Patch @vanillagreen/pi-tool-renderer so a TUI frame neither re-reads settings
files nor re-wraps unchanged tool chrome.

Pi re-renders the entire transcript on every frame, and this renderer runs its
chrome and user-message paths per message per frame. Two hot spots made
keystroke latency grow with transcript length: readPackageConfig parsed every
settings file on each call, and renderToolChromeLines re-wrapped every line of
every tool block on every render.

Applied by flake/packages.nix after npm install. To apply it to a development
checkout, run from the repository root:

  patch -p1 -d node_modules/@vanillagreen/pi-tool-renderer < patches/pi-tool-renderer-frame-cache.patch

Upstream: github.com/vanillagreencom/kendex

